  "description": "<p>You may access nearly 350 000 currently approved geographical names stored on the Canadian Geographical Names Data Base (CGNDB), Canada’s national bank of official geographical names. The CGNDB is the authoritative national database of Canada's geographical names. The purpose of the CGNDB is to store place names and their attributes that have been approved by the <a target='_blank' href='https://natural-resources.canada.ca/maps-tools-publications/maps/geographical-names-board-canada' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Geographical Names Board of Canada</a> (GNBC), the national coordinating body responsible for standards and policies on place names. The GNBC is comprised of members from each province and territory and various federal departments concerned with mapping, Indigenous lands, undersea features, national parks, archives, defence, translation, and statistics.&nbsp;</p><p>The CGNDB is maintained by <a target='_blank' href='https://natural-resources.canada.ca/' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Natural Resources Canada</a>, through the <a target='_blank' href='https://natural-resources.canada.ca/science-data/science-research/research-centres/canada-centre-mapping-earth-observation' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Canada Centre for Mapping and Earth Observation</a>. The geographic extent of the CGNDB is the Canadian landmass and water bodies; the temporal extent is from 1897 to present. The database includes the names of populated places and administrative areas, water features such as lakes, rivers and bays, terrain features like mountains, capes and valleys; and undersea features such as seamounts and trenches.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Content advisory:</strong> The Canadian Geographical Names Database contains historical terminology that is considered racist, offensive and derogatory. Geographical naming authorities are in the process of addressing many offensive place names, but the work is still ongoing. For more information, please contact the <a href='mailto:nrcan.geonames-Toponymes.rncan@canada.ca' rel='nofollow ugc'>GNBC Secretariat</a>.</p><p><strong>Source:</strong> <a target='_blank' href='https://natural-resources.canada.ca/maps-tools-publications/maps/geographical-names-canada/download-geographical-names-data' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>The Canadian Geographical Names Database</a>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Methodology:&nbsp;</strong>This service was created by taking the Canada .shp file and the Undersea &amp; Surface Maritime Features .shp file and publishing them within a single database.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Update Frequency:</strong> Quarterly&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Additional Resources:</strong></p><ul><li><a target='_blank' href='https://ftp.maps.canada.ca/pub/nrcan_rncan/vector/geobase_cgn_toponyme/doc/GeoBase_cgn_en_Specifications.pdf' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Canadian Geographical Names – CGN Product Specifications</a> - metadata document</li><li>Access the Canadian Geographical Names Database and learn about its content and attributes<a target='_blank' href='https://natural-resources.canada.ca/maps-tools-publications/tools-applications/canadian-geographical-names-database' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'> here</a></li></ul><p><strong>Contact information</strong></p><ul><li>For inquiries regarding the service, please leave a comment below</li><li>For inquiries on the data please contact:<ul><li>Land features: GNBC Secretariat (<a href='mailto:nrcan.geonames-toponymes.rncan@canada.ca' rel='nofollow ugc'>nrcan.geonames-toponymes.rncan@canada.ca</a>)</li><li>Undersea features: Advisory Committee on Undersea Feature Names, Canadian Hydrographic Service (<a href='mailto:ACUFN-CCNESM@dfo-mpo.gc.ca' rel='nofollow ugc'>ACUFN-CCNESM@dfo-mpo.gc.ca</a>)</li></ul></li></ul><p>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>Vous pouvez accéder à près de 350 000 noms géographiques actuellement approuvés, conservés dans la Base de données toponymiques du Canada (BDTC), la banque nationale de noms géographiques officiels du Canada. La Base de données toponymiques du Canada (BDTC) constitue la référence nationale en matière de noms géographiques canadiens. Elle a pour vocation de conserver les noms de lieux et leurs attributs approuvés par la<a target='_blank' href='https://ressources-naturelles.canada.ca/carte-outils-publications/cartes/commission-toponymie-canada?_gl=1*13cm6zf*_ga*MTM5NjIzNTQ1MS4xNzUyNzYzMTgx*_ga_C2N57Y7DX5*czE3ODQ4MjI0ODAkbzEyJGcxJHQxNzg0ODIzNDQ2JGo2MCRsMCRoMA..' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'> Commission de toponymie du Canada</a> (CTC), l'organisme national de coordination chargé des normes et des politiques relatives aux noms géographiques. La CTC se compose de membres représentant chaque province et territoire ainsi que divers ministères fédéraux dont les domaines d'activité touchent à la cartographie, aux terres autochtones, aux entités sous-marines, aux parcs nationaux, aux archives, à la défense, à la traduction et aux statistiques.</p><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>&nbsp;</div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>La BDTC est gérée par <a target='_blank' href='https://ressources-naturelles.canada.ca/' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Ressources naturelles Canada</a>, par l’intermédiaire du <a target='_blank' href='https://ressources-naturelles.canada.ca/science-donnees/science-recherche/centre-recherche/centre-canadien-cartographie-observation-terre?_gl=1*1lt9amf*_ga*MTM5NjIzNTQ1MS4xNzUyNzYzMTgx*_ga_C2N57Y7DX5*czE3ODQ4MjI0ODAkbzEyJGcxJHQxNzg0ODIzNDk2JGoxMCRsMCRoMA..' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Centre canadien de cartographie et d’observation de la Terre.</a> L’étendue géographique de la BDTC englobe la masse continentale du Canada et ses étendues d’eau, tandis que l’étendue temporelle couvre la période de 1897 à aujourd’hui.</div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>&nbsp;</div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><strong>Mise en garde:</strong> La base de données toponymiques du Canada contient des termes historiques considérés comme racistes, offensants et péjoratifs. Les autorités de dénomination géographique travaillent actuellement à l'élimination de nombreux toponymes offensants, mais le travail est toujours en cours. Pour obtenir plus de renseignements, veuillez communiquer avec <a href='mailto:nrcan.geonames-Toponymes.rncan@canada.ca' rel='nofollow ugc'>le secrétariat de la CTC</a>.</div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>&nbsp;</div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><strong>Source:</strong> <a target='_blank' href='https://ressources-naturelles.canada.ca/carte-outils-publications/cartes/toponymes-canada/telechargement-donnees-toponymiques?_gl=1*cca8s2*_ga*MTM5NjIzNTQ1MS4xNzUyNzYzMTgx*_ga_C2N57Y7DX5*czE3ODQ4MjI0ODAkbzEyJGcxJHQxNzg0ODIyODQwJGo1JGwwJGgw' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>La Base de données toponymiques du Canada&nbsp;</a></div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>&nbsp;</div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><strong>Méthodologie:</strong> Ce service a été créé en utilisant le fichier .shp du Canada et le fichier .shp des entités maritimes sous-marines et de surface, puis en les publiant au sein d'une base de données unique.</div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>&nbsp;</div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><strong>Fréquence de mise à jour: </strong>trimestriellement</div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>&nbsp;</div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><strong>Ressources supplémentaires :</strong></div><ul><li><a target='_blank' href='https://ftp.maps.canada.ca/pub/nrcan_rncan/vector/geobase_cgn_toponyme/doc/GeoBase_tc_fr_Specifications.pdf' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Toponymes canadiens – TC Spécifications de produit</a> - document de métadonnées</li><li>Accédez à la Base de données toponymiques du Canada, découvrez son contenu, et ses champs <a target='_blank' href='https://ressources-naturelles.canada.ca/carte-outils-publications/outils-logiciels/base-donnees-toponymiques-canada?_gl=1*1uuhoyk*_ga*MTM5NjIzNTQ1MS4xNzUyNzYzMTgx*_ga_C2N57Y7DX5*czE3ODQ4MjI0ODAkbzEyJGcxJHQxNzg0ODIzODI0JGo1NiRsMCRoMA..' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>ici</a></li></ul><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>&nbsp;</div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border-style:solid; border-width:0px; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><strong>Coordonnées:</strong></div><ul><li><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:medium;'><font style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'>Pour toute demande concernant le service, veuillez laisser un commentaire ci-dessous</span></font></span></li><li><span style='background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(74,74,74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:15px;'><span style='display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>Les questions concernant les données doivent être adressées:</span></span><ul><li>Caractéristiques du terrain : Secrétariat de la CTC (<a href='mailto:nrcan.geonames-toponymes.rncan@canada.ca' rel='nofollow ugc'>nrcan.geonames-toponymes.rncan@canada.ca</a>)</li><li>Caractéristiques sous-marines : Comité consultatif des noms d'entités sous-marines<br />Service hydrographique du Canada (<a href='mailto:ACUFN-CCNESM@dfo-mpo.gc.ca' rel='nofollow ugc'>ACUFN-CCNESM@dfo-mpo.gc.ca</a>)</li></ul></li></ul>",
